From f8edaf6fbf3fa18aa3ae2c494a2b5ed28db18067 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Fishlock <alex.fishlock@racingjag.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 14:54:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Migrate the Lyngdorf number platform to the lyngdorf 2.0
 API

Trims are a mapping of controls in 2.0 rather than a per-band triple of
attributes, so the six trims become one lookup each and the entity
description loses a field.

range_fn stays the test for whether the model has a control. On the 1.11
pin lipsync also reads None until the device reports a value, and
connect() does not wait for that, so keying entity creation off the
control would drop the entity at startup.
